  "id": "DrugBank_DB01204 - MONDO_17893",
  "verbalization": "Mitoxantrone is associated with Inherited Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML) through a chain of indications that involve unclassified AML, which in turn is linked to specific drugs. The evidence suggests that Mitoxantrone may be repurposed for treating AML, as it is indicated for unclassified AML, which is a broad category that encompasses a variety of subtypes. This unclassified status implies that Mitoxantrone may have a role in the treatment of AML, though it is not yet classified as a specific therapy. The presence of multiple drugs—such as tioguanine, ivosidenib, and decitabine—that are indicated for unclassified AML further supports the idea that Mitoxantrone may be part of a broader therapeutic strategy for this condition. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Mitoxantrone to be used in the treatment of inherited AML, though the exact mechanism of action remains unclear and requires further investigation.",
